/*
  sdi_vw_dashboardPulseTms_bronze_appendix_wide
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  PulseTMS dashboard appendix (Bronze): metric definitions + glossary,
  wide/denormalized, one row per apx_id. Ported from BigQuery's
  vw_sdi_pulse_bronze_pulseTab1_appendix.

  Static reference/config data -- no upstream fact source, no incremental
  key, no incremental logic needed. This is a VIEW: every query
  re-evaluates the full literal set, so there is no backfill step,
  ever, for this model.

  Port notes (BQ -> Databricks):
  - No BQ-specific functions are used anywhere in this file (pure
    UNION ALL of typed literals) so nothing needed translating beyond
    this config block -- every SELECT below is byte-for-byte the same
    literal values as the BQ source, except the two content changes
    noted below.
  - Validated programmatically before porting (49 rows, 27 columns each,
    consistent column order; apx_id unique across all 49 rows;
    apx_parent_id / apx_cvr_numerator_id / apx_cvr_denominator_id all
    resolve to a real apx_id in this same set; apx_is_subflow = TRUE
    iff apx_parent_id is populated; apx_build_labels/apx_build_details
    and apx_excl_labels/apx_excl_details have matching \n-delimited
    bullet counts per row -- this last one matters because Silver
    zips label/detail pairs positionally, so a mismatch here would
    have silently misaligned bullets downstream).
  - CAUTION for future edits: Databricks/Spark gives a bare integer
    literal (e.g. `1`) INT (32-bit) by default, where BigQuery's INT64
    default is 64-bit. Harmless at this row count, but if apx_sort_order
    values are ever driven from a join/expression instead of a literal,
    cast explicitly to BIGINT to avoid a silent type mismatch against
    Silver's placeholder columns (Silver already casts around this --
    see that model's header).

  Content changes made post-port (confirmed with Khalid, not in the
  original BQ source -- re-validated after applying, same checks as above,
  all still pass):
  - 'exit_traffic_door_swings' (apx_id) moved from Mid Funnel to Top
    Funnel: apx_funnel_stage / apx_funnel_sort changed, nothing else
    about that row touched.
  - New row added: apx_id 'new_bans_digital_pct_of_activations',
    apx_sort_order 50, Bottom Funnel / 'New BANs' category -- Digital %
    of New BAN Activations (Digital Unassisted / (Digital Unassisted +
    VR New BANs)). This is a derived ratio, not a count, so
    apx_cvr_numerator_id/apx_cvr_denominator_id are left NULL (that
    wiring is single-id/single-id and can't represent a summed
    denominator) -- the formula is spelled out in apx_build_labels/
    apx_build_details instead, same as how this same % already lived as
    a build-detail bullet inside 'new_bans_digital_unassisted' (row 23,
    "PCT OF CONSUMER") before being promoted to its own row. That bullet
    was left as-is in row 23, so the same figure is now documented in
    two places -- worth deduplicating later if that bothers you.
    Placed at apx_sort_order 50 (after the Glossary block) rather than
    renumbering the Glossary rows down by one: the dashboard groups by
    apx_funnel_stage_key first and sorts by apx_sort_order only within
    that group (that's what Gold's apx_funnel_stage_key exists for), so
    a non-contiguous sort_order is harmless for display -- it just means
    "row 25-49 = Glossary" is no longer a reliable assumption to hardcode
    anywhere. Nothing in Bronze/Silver/Gold currently relies on that
    range being contiguous (all filtering is by apx_record_type), but
    flagging it here since it's the kind of assumption that's easy to
    bake into a future query without noticing.

  Source-table lineage updated to Databricks (this pass) -- apx_source_
  system/apx_source_platform/apx_source_table now describe where each
  metric's number actually comes from post-port, not the old BQ paths:
  - MFC (rows 1-2) and QGP-sourced rows (VR Calls/Chats, Exit Traffic,
    New BANs - Digital Unassisted, VR New BANs, Digital % of New BAN
    Activations) were ALREADY pointing at real, current Databricks
    tables even in the original BQ-era appendix (raw_media_flowchart and
    prdrzrlakehouse.qgp_restricted.qgpweeklyview respectively, both
    confirmed still current) -- left untouched.
  - UPV Actuals + Postpaid/HSI/BYOD flows (rows 3, 5-7), Add to Cart
    (rows 11-14), and all 8 Orders rows (15-22): all confirmed by Khalid
    to come from the same table -- prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_
    adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly. UPV Actuals
    and Cart/Orders were confirmed directly; the UPV/Cart/Orders
    sub-flow rows were extended from those confirmations since they're
    the same table sliced by channel group, not independently confirmed
    row by row. The old Improvado raw-table references (adobe_cs_day_tmo,
    sdi_raw_adobe_pp_pulse_pro_orders_unassisted_daily_tmo) are no longer
    used here -- that data now reaches the dashboard through the curated
    Gold table instead of being read directly.
  - UPV Forecasts (row 4): now resolved -- apx_source_table points to
    prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_dashboardPulseTms_silver_upvForecast_
    weekly (this metric's own Silver table; it doesn't feed the shared
    adobeFunnel Gold table the other 16 rows use, it only reaches Gold
    via sdi_vw_dashboardPulseTms_gold_unified_long downstream). Per the
    actual procedure Khalid shared, the old "spend-indexed proxy"
    methodology described in apx_build_labels/apx_build_details/
    apx_sum_warning/apx_excl_labels/apx_excl_details was fully stale and
    has been rewritten: Bronze is populated by a manual CSV upload via a
    Databricks notebook (upvForecast_bronze_upload.py, ad hoc, not on a
    schedule) until the forecasting team has a proper feed; Silver
    currently passes the Bronze value straight through for the "All
    Channels" grain only and returns NULL for every other channel_group
    (temporary, pending per-channel forecasts). apx_refresh_cadence set
    to 'Manual / ad hoc - after each quarterly CSV upload' accordingly
    -- this one is NOT on the 'Daily at 7 AM PST' cadence the other 16
    rows share, since it isn't the same pipeline.

  Refresh cadence + consolidation note (this pass) -- applies to the 16
  rows sourced from sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannel
  Groups_weekly (UPV Actuals + 3 flows, Add to Cart + 3 flows, Orders
  Unassisted + 3 flows, Orders Assisted + 3 flows -- NOT UPV Forecasts,
  still unresolved per above):
  - apx_refresh_cadence set to 'Daily at 7 AM PST' on all 16, confirmed
    by Khalid. The 4 "overall" rows (UPV Actuals, Add to Cart Overall,
    Orders Unassisted, Orders Assisted) also had their own trailing
    REFRESH bullet inside apx_build_details updated to match -- it
    previously read the old cadence ("Weekly - notebook run" / "Daily
    at 9 AM PT"), which would otherwise have contradicted the
    apx_refresh_cadence column sitting right next to it.
  - A new leading bullet, "SOURCE ARCHITECTURE", added to
    apx_build_labels/apx_build_details on all 16: notes that the Gold
    flowPerformance table consolidates the individually migrated/ported
    Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all
    Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place -- this is architecture
    context, not filter logic, so it's placed first in the bullet list
    on every row rather than mixed in with the LAYER/CONDITION filter
    bullets that follow.

  "Pulse 1.2" content refresh (this pass) -- the team's authoritative
  metric-appendix spreadsheet was merged in. Summary of what changed:

  - Enriched apx_build_labels/apx_build_details on the 16 flowPerformance
    rows (UPV, Cart, Orders + their sub-flows) and on Eligibility Checks
    with exact Adobe field codes (v6, v18, v35, v45, v82, v94, v100,
    v103, v121, v154, v155, e4, etc.) and exact quoted page-name/segment
    strings that the appendix previously only described loosely. Every
    label/detail pair was rebuilt as a matched (label, detail) list
    rather than hand-edited as two separate strings, specifically to
    rule out the kind of positional mismatch that's easy to introduce
    when a bullet list grows -- validated after the fact regardless.
  - New row: Eligibility Checks Completed (Mid Funnel, HSI, apx_sort_
    order 50). Per the team doc this pipeline is explicitly NOT YET BUILT
    -- apx_source_table, apx_refresh_cadence, and apx_sum_warning all say
    PENDING rather than pointing at a real table, so the dashboard
    doesn't present this as live before it is. Update those three fields
    once the pipeline ships.
  - New BANs "digital %" is now THREE separate, QGP-precalculated metrics
    (Digital % of Phone New Account Activations -- Total / No Assistance
    / Assistance; apx_sort_order 51-53; sourced from prdrzranalytics.
    lab42.sdi_tbl_qgparchive_gold_curated_weekly), replacing the single
    row this file previously invented (new_bans_digital_pct_of_
    activations, computed locally as Digital Unassisted / (Digital
    Unassisted + VR New BANs)). That inferred computation is NOT what the
    team's real metric does -- the real ratio has a different, more
    precise denominator (excludes National Retail Indirect) and only the
    Total variant carries a QGP target. The old row's "PCT OF CONSUMER"
    bullet inside New BANs - Digital Unassisted (row 23) has been
    replaced with a pointer to these three rows instead of a second,
    now-inconsistent self-computed percentage.
  - UPV Forecasts (row 4): the team's Pulse 1.2 doc still describes the
    OLD spend-indexed-proxy methodology for this metric -- the same text
    that was already replaced last pass based on the actual current
    stored procedure (sdi_sp_dashboardPulseTms_silver_upvForecast_
    weekly), which implements a materially different, simpler method
    (manual CSV upload, All Channels passthrough, other channels NULL).
    This is a genuine doc/code conflict, not something to silently
    resolve either way -- row 4 was left on the procedure-based content
    from last pass. Worth someone confirming with the forecasting/doc
    owner whether Pulse 1.2 just hasn't caught up yet, or whether the
    procedure itself is mid-migration and the old method is coming back.
  - Per Khalid: all Adobe-sourced rows (UPV, Cart, Orders, Eligibility
    Checks) use prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_
    flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly (Eligibility Checks excepted,
    still PENDING per above) even though the team doc's own Data Source
    column says sdi_vw_dashboardpulsetms_gold_unified_long for these
    rows -- that's a deliberate, confirmed override, not an oversight.
  - A handful of one-liner and glossary definitions were enriched with
    small clarifying clauses the team doc added (Exit Traffic, Orders
    Assisted, [sdi] Activation Intent, Assisted, QTD) -- substance
    unchanged, wording tightened to match the current source of record.

  Naming clarity fix (this pass) -- rows 16-18 (the Orders Postpaid/HSI/
  BYOD sub-flows under Orders (Unassisted)) never actually said
  "Unassisted" in their apx_id or apx_label, while their siblings under
  Orders (Assisted) -- rows 20-22 -- always said "Assisted" explicitly.
  That asymmetry is genuinely confusing when scanning the row list (it's
  what prompted Khalid to think a few Orders rows were missing entirely).
  Renamed both id and label to match the Assisted side's pattern:
    orders_postpaid_flow -> orders_unassisted_postpaid_flow
      'Orders - Postpaid Flow' -> 'Orders Unassisted - Postpaid Flow'
    orders_hsi_flow -> orders_unassisted_hsi_flow
      'Orders - HSI Flow' -> 'Orders Unassisted - HSI Flow'
    orders_byod_flow -> orders_unassisted_byod_flow
      'Orders - BYOD Flow' -> 'Orders Unassisted - BYOD Flow'
  Confirmed safe before renaming: nothing else in this file referenced
  these three apx_ids via apx_parent_id/apx_cvr_numerator_id/apx_cvr_
  denominator_id except each row's own self-referencing
  apx_cvr_numerator_id, which was updated along with the id. Also fixed
  the now-stale prose that named these sub-flows by their old label,
  wherever it appeared: the CVR-formula and "Sums with .../Part of ..."
  lines inside these 3 rows' own apx_build_details/apx_sum_warning, and
  the "DERIVED TOTAL" bullet inside row 15 (orders_unassisted_overall)
  that lists all three sub-flow names. If you're wiring a Tableau
  parameter or filter off apx_id for these rows, it needs re-pointing
  at the new ids.

  New third hierarchy level added (this pass) -- at Khalid's request:
  Orders (Overall) is now a real row (apx_id orders_overall, apx_sort_
  order 54, category 'Orders') sitting above the existing Orders
  (Unassisted) and Orders (Assisted) rows, matching how Add to Cart
  (Overall) already works for the Cart family:
    Orders (Overall)
      |- Orders (Unassisted)            [now apx_is_subflow=TRUE,
      |    |- ...Postpaid/HSI/BYOD          apx_parent_id=orders_overall]
      |- Orders (Assisted)              [now apx_is_subflow=TRUE,
           |- ...Postpaid/HSI/BYOD          apx_parent_id=orders_overall]
  Before this, both Unassisted and Assisted were flat top-level rows
  (apx_parent_id NULL) with no combined total above them at all.
  Reciprocal apx_sum_warning added to both: each now states it sums
  with the other to equal Orders (Overall).
  CAUTION -- one bullet in Orders (Overall)'s own apx_build_details
  (labeled BASE METRIC) is Claude's inference, not an independently
  confirmed fact: it describes the base Orders-confirmation-page
  population as the union of what Unassisted/Assisted split via their
  proxy segments, reasoned from those two being documented as using
  "the exact same signals" but one including and one excluding them.
  Logically sound given how those two are already documented, but
  nobody has independently confirmed there's a real, separately-named
  Adobe segment behind it -- worth a quick sanity check with whoever
  owns the adobeFunnel Gold table before treating that specific bullet
  as gospel.
  Category choice: the new row got its own category ('Orders') rather
  than being folded into 'Orders Unassisted'/'Orders Assisted', which
  stayed as-is on the 8 existing rows -- unlike Add to Cart, where the
  parent and all 3 children share one category. Category is a separate
  dimension from the parent_id/is_subflow hierarchy (doesn't affect
  it), so this doesn't break anything, but flagging the asymmetry in
  case you want full Cart-parity later.
  apx_sort_order 54 was chosen for the same reason 50-53 were: it's
  outside the dashboard's current flat-list Metric-dropdown design (no
  visual parent/child nesting is built yet, so exact numeric position
  among Bottom Funnel rows doesn't matter for display today). If a
  future version of the dashboard nests children under parents visually
  using apx_parent_id, revisit this number so Orders (Overall) sorts
  ahead of its own children instead of trailing everything else in
  Bottom Funnel.

  Maintenance: to add a metric or glossary term, append a new SELECT
  with the next unused apx_sort_order and a new, unique apx_id (place it
  wherever reads best in this file -- physical order here doesn't affect
  output, the final ORDER BY does), then
  re-run this CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW statement.
*/

CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_vw_dashboardPulseTms_bronze_appendix_wide
COMMENT 'PulseTMS dashboard appendix (Bronze): metric definitions + glossary, wide/denormalized, one row per apx_id. Static reference data, no upstream source.'
AS
SELECT * FROM(
SELECT 1 AS apx_sort_order,'mfc_spend_postpaid' AS apx_id,'MFC Spend - Postpaid' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Media Spend' AS apx_category,1 AS apx_category_sort,'Postpaid LOB' AS apx_scope,'Postpaid' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Media Flow Chart (MFC)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.raw_media_flowchart' AS apx_source_table,'Amy Pritchett / Will Butler' AS apx_data_owner,'Weekly - finalized 3 PM PT Friday' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Total dollars invested in Postpaid media each week, as tracked and finalized by LOB teams in the Media Flow Chart.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE & QA\nLOB TEAMS\nUPDATES\nTACTIC FILTER\nCHANNEL FILTER\nFORECASTED SPEND\nACT VS FCST %\nQTD SUM' AS apx_build_labels,'Media Flow Chart (MFC) - T-Mobile centralized media spend source of truth, stored in Databricks.\nContribute Postpaid spend data each Thursday. QA and finalization by 3 PM PT Friday.\nWill Butler team performs twice-weekly updates for mid-week corrections.\nGlobal selector affecting all spend rows.\nApplies to MFC Spend only - does not affect any other metric.\nPlanned/budgeted amount from MFC.\n(Actuals minus Forecast) / Forecast.\nRunning total of weekly actuals from Q2 start.' AS apx_build_details,'MICRO EXCLUSION' AS apx_excl_labels,'Excludes Message_Type = MICRO and Message values SEM Postpaid/Micro and Micro Postpaid Offers until channel mapping is finalized.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 2 AS apx_sort_order,'mfc_spend_broadband' AS apx_id,'MFC Spend - Broadband' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Media Spend' AS apx_category,2 AS apx_category_sort,'Broadband / HSI LOB' AS apx_scope,'HSI' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Media Flow Chart (MFC)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.raw_media_flowchart' AS apx_source_table,'Amy Pritchett / Will Butler' AS apx_data_owner,'Weekly - finalized 3 PM PT Friday' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Total dollars invested in Broadband (Home Internet) media each week, as tracked and finalized in the Media Flow Chart.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE\nLOB TEAMS\nAGGREGATION\nFORECASTED SPEND\nACT VS FCST %' AS apx_build_labels,'Same source and build logic as MFC Spend - Postpaid, filtered to the Broadband LOB.\nSame LOB contribution, QA, and refresh cadence as Postpaid spend.\nAggregates weekly spend across all channels for the Broadband / HSI line of business.\nPlanned/budgeted Broadband amount.\n(Actuals minus Forecast) / Forecast.' AS apx_build_details,'MICRO EXCLUSION' AS apx_excl_labels,'Same MICRO message type exclusions as Postpaid MFC Spend.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 3 AS apx_sort_order,'UPV_actuals_overall' AS apx_id,'UPV Actuals (Overall)' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'UPV' AS apx_category,3 AS apx_category_sort,'All Flows Combined' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,FALSE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Khalid / Ben' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Count of distinct website visitors who landed on T-Mobile.com and engaged beyond their first page - the broadest measure of qualified prospect traffic entering the funnel.' AS apx_definition,'IMPORTANT: Cannot sum Postpaid + HSI + BYOD flows to equal this total. Adobe deduplicates Unique Visitors at the scope of the metric.' AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nUNIVERSAL FILTERS\nLAYER 1\nLAYER 2\nLAYER 3\nLAYER 4\nNO FLOW FILTER\nWOW %\nAVG OF QTD\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nDDM Exclude Data Issue + [DA] Web Visits + [sdi] Postpaid (Exclude TFB).\nExclude TMO Mobile Network Carrier - removes VISITS where Mobile Carrier Network = T-Mobile.\n[sdi] Exclude Authenticated or Network Authenticated VISITS - removes sessions where User State = Authenticated or Network Authenticated, or any LOA token (LOA0.5 to LOA3) is present.\n[sdi] Exclude Visit Login Page - removes VISITS where Page URL - Full (v103) contains associated_billing_accounts, t-mobile.com/guest-pay, or account.t-mobile.com/signin/v2/.\n[DA] Exclude Single Page Visits - removes VISITS where Single Page Visits exists. Enforces the Non-Bounced qualifier.\nBroadest universe across all product areas.\n(Current week minus Prior week) / Prior week.\nRunning average of weekly actuals from Q2 start.\nDaily at 7 AM PST.' AS apx_build_details,'T-MOBILE NETWORK VISITORS\nAUTHENTICATED/LOA SESSIONS\nLOGIN & GUEST-PAY PAGES\nSINGLE-PAGE BOUNCES\nNATIVE APP TRAFFIC\nTFB PAGES' AS apx_excl_labels,'Visitors on the T-Mobile cellular network.\nAll sessions where User State = Authenticated or any LOA token present.\nAll visits touching sign-in or guest-pay pages.\nSessions with only one page view.\niOS/Android T-Life, MyT-Mobile, Metro app sessions.\nb2b, Atwork, /business, /t-priority URL paths.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 4 AS apx_sort_order,'UPV_forecasts' AS apx_id,'UPV Forecasts' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'UPV' AS apx_category,4 AS apx_category_sort,'All Flows' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,FALSE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe UPV forecast -> Databricks (manual upload)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_dashboardPulseTms_silver_upvForecast_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Khalid / Ben' AS apx_data_owner,'Manual / ad hoc - after each quarterly CSV upload' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'A modeled weekly estimate of expected UPV, used to benchmark whether actual traffic is tracking ahead or behind plan.' AS apx_definition,'Populated for the "All Channels" grain only -- Direct, Organic Search, Paid Search, Paid Social, Programmatic, and Other all return NULL until the forecasting team''s channel-level UPV forecast becomes available. Do not expect this to reconcile against channel-level actuals.' AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE\nUPLOAD METHOD\nCHANNEL ALLOCATION\nALL CHANNELS\nOTHER CHANNELS\nBOUNDARY WEEKS\nWOW %\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'Adobe UPV forecast, uploaded manually by the forecasting team - not derived from Adobe Analytics segment data directly.\nBronze table sdi_tbl_dashboardPulseTms_bronze_upvForecast_weekly is populated via a Databricks notebook (upvForecast_bronze_upload.py) with a manual CSV upload, run ad hoc after each quarterly forecast is received.\nSilver applies a channel allocation ratio: All Channels = 1.0 (full passthrough of the Bronze value); every other channel_group = NULL, until per-channel forecasts are available from the forecasting team.\nAll Channels metric_value = Bronze upv_forecast value, unchanged.\nDirect, Organic Search, Paid Search, Paid Social, Programmatic, Other all return NULL for this metric until channel-level forecasts exist.\nBronze values are already boundary-week-prorated by the upload notebook - Silver applies no additional x days_in_period / 7 adjustment.\n(Current week minus Prior week) / Prior week, using the standard WoW self-join pattern shared with every other Silver table.\nManual/ad hoc, after each quarterly CSV upload via the upvForecast_bronze_upload.py notebook - not on the daily/weekly automated schedule.' AS apx_build_details,'CHANNEL BREAKOUTS\nMANUAL PROCESS' AS apx_excl_labels,'Non-"All Channels" channel_group rows are excluded (NULL) until per-channel forecasts exist - not a data quality issue, a known and expected gap.\nNot an automated pipeline - depends on a person manually uploading a CSV via the Databricks notebook each quarter; can lag if that upload is late.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 5 AS apx_sort_order,'UPV_postpaid_flow' AS apx_id,'UPV - Postpaid Flow' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'UPV' AS apx_category,5 AS apx_category_sort,'Postpaid' AS apx_scope,'Postpaid' AS apx_lob,TRUE AS apx_is_subflow,'UPV_actuals_overall' AS apx_parent_id,FALSE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Khalid / Ben' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Distinct non-bounced visitors who browsed the core Postpaid phone/plan shopping experience, with HSI pages excluded.' AS apx_definition,'Cannot be summed with HSI and BYOD flows to equal UPV Actuals.' AS apx_sum_warning,'cart_postpaid_flow' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_postpaid_flow' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nLAYER 1\nLAYER 2\nLAYER 3 - HSI EXCLUSION\nHSI PAGE NAME\nHSI PAGE URL\nHSI SITE SECTION\nHSI PRODUCT TYPE\nBYOD NOTE\nCVR DENOMINATOR' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nUniversal filters.\nProspect qualifiers: Exclude TMO Mobile Network Carrier + [sdi] Exclude Authenticated + [sdi] Exclude Visit Login Page + [DA] Exclude Single Page Visits.\n[sdi] Postpaid Flow (Exclude HSI + BYOD) - HIT-level exclusion removing any hit matching HSI identifiers.\nPage Name contains "TLife App | Shop : HINT", "TMO | HINT", or "TMO:UNO | HINT".\nPage URL contains www.t-mobile.com/isp, es.t-mobile.com/home-internet, www.t-mobile.com/home-internet, or www.t-mobile.com/stores/bd/home-internet.\nSite Name = TMO AND Site Section (v1) = HINT.\nPage Name contains "TLife App | Shop" OR "TMO | Shop" AND Product Type (v100) = ISP.\nBYOD SIM pages are NOT excluded at UPV level - excluded at cart and orders only.\nUsed as denominator for Cart Postpaid CVR% and Orders Postpaid CVR%.' AS apx_build_details,'HSI PAGE HITS\nPROSPECT FILTERS' AS apx_excl_labels,'All hits matching HINT page names, /isp/ and /home-internet/ URLs, Site Section = HINT, Product Type = ISP.\nAll Layer 2 prospect filters also applied.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 6 AS apx_sort_order,'UPV_hsi_flow' AS apx_id,'UPV - HSI Flow' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'UPV' AS apx_category,6 AS apx_category_sort,'Home Internet (HSI)' AS apx_scope,'HSI' AS apx_lob,TRUE AS apx_is_subflow,'UPV_actuals_overall' AS apx_parent_id,FALSE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Khalid / Ben' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Distinct non-bounced visitors who browsed T-Mobile Home Internet pages - the prospect audience for the internet service offering.' AS apx_definition,'Cannot be summed with Postpaid and BYOD flows to equal UPV Actuals.' AS apx_sum_warning,'cart_hsi_flow' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_hsi_flow' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nLAYER 1\nLAYER 2\nLAYER 3 - HSI INCLUSION\nHSI PAGE NAME\nHSI PAGE URL\nHSI SITE SECTION\nHSI PRODUCT TYPE\nCVR DENOMINATOR' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nUniversal filters.\nProspect qualifiers (same as UPV Actuals).\n[DA] HSI Any HSI Site Page Hits - HIT-level inclusion where any hit matched HSI identifiers.\nPage Name contains "TLife App | Shop : HINT", "TMO | HINT", or "TMO:UNO | HINT".\nPage URL contains www.t-mobile.com/isp, es.t-mobile.com/home-internet, www.t-mobile.com/home-internet, or www.t-mobile.com/stores/bd/home-internet.\nSite Name = TMO AND Site Section (v1) = HINT.\nPage Name contains "TLife App | Shop" OR "TMO | Shop" AND Product Type (v100) = ISP.\nUsed as denominator for Cart HSI CVR% and Orders HSI CVR%.' AS apx_build_details,'SCOPE\nMUTUAL EXCLUSIVITY' AS apx_excl_labels,'Scoped to visits containing any HSI page hit. All prospect filters applied.\nNot mutually exclusive from Postpaid or BYOD at visit level.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 7 AS apx_sort_order,'UPV_byod_flow' AS apx_id,'UPV - BYOD Flow' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'UPV' AS apx_category,7 AS apx_category_sort,'BYOD' AS apx_scope,'BYOD' AS apx_lob,TRUE AS apx_is_subflow,'UPV_actuals_overall' AS apx_parent_id,FALSE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Khalid / Ben' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Distinct non-bounced visitors who browsed BYOD or device-switching pages - prospects exploring how to bring an existing device to T-Mobile.' AS apx_definition,'Cannot be summed with Postpaid and HSI flows to equal UPV Actuals.' AS apx_sum_warning,'cart_byod_flow' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_byod_flow' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nLAYER 1\nLAYER 2\nLAYER 3 - BYOD PAGES\nPAGE 1\nPAGE 2\nPAGE 3\nPAGE 4 (CONTAINS)\nPAGE 5\nPAGE 6 (HITS)\nPAGE 7 (HITS)\nPAGE 8 (HITS)\nPAGE 9 (HITS)\nCVR DENOMINATOR' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nUniversal filters.\nProspect qualifiers (same as UPV Actuals).\nBYOD Pages - Visits. Includes visits where any page name or hit matched BYOD identifiers.\nPage Name = "TMO | Shop : Browse : Bring Your Own Phone".\nPage Name = "TMO | Support : Resources : Switch from Current Carrier".\nPage Name = "TMO | Shop : Browse : Bring your own phone eligibility checker".\nPage Name contains "TMO | Shop : switch :".\nPage Name = "TMO | Marketing : Landing Page : Quick Prospect Switching".\nPage Name = "TMO | Shop : Cell Phone Detail : T-Mobile SIM Card" (HITS).\nPage Name = "TLife App | Shop : Cell Phone Detail : T-Mobile SIM Card" (HITS).\nPage Name = "TLife App | Shop : Tablet Detail : Mobile Internet SIM Card" (HITS).\nPage Name = "TMO | Shop : Tablet Detail : T-Mobile Mobile Internet SIM Card" (HITS).\nUsed as denominator for Cart BYOD CVR% and Orders BYOD CVR%.' AS apx_build_details,'SCOPE\nMUTUAL EXCLUSIVITY' AS apx_excl_labels,'Scoped to visits containing any BYOD or SIM card page hit. All prospect filters applied.\nNot mutually exclusive from other flows at visit level.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 8 AS apx_sort_order,'vr_calls' AS apx_id,'VR Calls' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Mid Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,2 AS apx_funnel_sort,'VR Actions' AS apx_category,8 AS apx_category_sort,'All / Postpaid' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Quarterly Game Plan (QGP)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzrlakehouse.qgp_restricted.qgpweeklyview' AS apx_source_table,'Preeti Laharwani / Bharat Kavuru' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 9 AM PT' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Phone calls placed by customers clicking a T-Mobile.com phone number to get live sales help - a direct signal of high purchase intent.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE\nHOW IT IS BUILT\nTRIGGER\nFORECAST\nACT VS FCST %\nQTD SUM\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'QGP operational data - entirely separate from Adobe Analytics. No Adobe segment filtering applies.\nCounts customer calls handled by T-Mobile Virtual Retail (VR) sales teams.\nTriggered when a customer clicks a phone number on T-Mobile.com to get assistance purchasing a device or plan.\nQGP provides both weekly actuals and a weekly forecast (VR Calls QGP).\n(Actuals minus QGP Forecast) / QGP Forecast.\nRunning total from Q2 start.\nDaily at 9 AM PT.' AS apx_build_details,'ADOBE FILTERING' AS apx_excl_labels,'No Adobe segment filtering. QGP operational data only.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 9 AS apx_sort_order,'vr_chats' AS apx_id,'VR Chats' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Mid Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,2 AS apx_funnel_sort,'VR Actions' AS apx_category,9 AS apx_category_sort,'All / Postpaid' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Quarterly Game Plan (QGP)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzrlakehouse.qgp_restricted.qgpweeklyview' AS apx_source_table,'Preeti Laharwani / Bharat Kavuru' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 9 AM PT' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Chat conversations initiated by customers on T-Mobile.com with Virtual Retail sales agents - indicating purchase-ready engagement.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE\nHOW IT IS BUILT\nTRIGGER\nFORECAST\nACT VS FCST %\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'QGP operational data - no Adobe segment filtering.\nCounts customer chat conversations handled by T-Mobile VR sales teams.\nTriggered when a customer clicks to chat on T-Mobile.com to get help purchasing a device or plan.\nQGP provides both actuals and a weekly forecast.\n(Actuals minus QGP Forecast) / QGP Forecast.\nDaily at 9 AM PT.' AS apx_build_details,'ADOBE FILTERING' AS apx_excl_labels,'No Adobe segment filtering. QGP operational data only.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 10 AS apx_sort_order,'exit_traffic_door_swings' AS apx_id,'Exit Traffic (Door Swings)' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Top Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,1 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Retail Actions' AS apx_category,10 AS apx_category_sort,'Retail' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Quarterly Game Plan (QGP)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzrlakehouse.qgp_restricted.qgpweeklyview' AS apx_source_table,'Preeti Laharwani / Bharat Kavuru' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 9 AM PT' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Total customer entries/exits at T-Mobile retail stores each week, measured by door-swing sensors - a proxy for offline foot traffic driven by digital awareness.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE\nHOW IT IS BUILT\nDATA COLLECTION\nFORECAST\nACT VS FCST %\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'QGP operational data sourced from retail door-swing sensor hardware - no Adobe segment filtering.\nCounts physical customer exits from T-Mobile retail store locations.\nData sourced from door-swing sensor readings at store entrances/exits, reported through QGP.\nQGP provides both actuals and a weekly forecast.\n(Actuals minus QGP Forecast) / QGP Forecast.\nDaily at 9 AM PT.' AS apx_build_details,'ADOBE FILTERING\nPURCHASE OUTCOME' AS apx_excl_labels,'Retail sensor data - no Adobe filtering.\nCounts all store visits regardless of purchase outcome.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 11 AS apx_sort_order,'add_to_cart_overall' AS apx_id,'Add to Cart (Overall)' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Mid Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,2 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Cart' AS apx_category,11 AS apx_category_sort,'Postpaid + HSI + BYOD' AS apx_scope,'All' AS apx_lob,FALSE AS apx_is_subflow,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Improvado' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Total visits in which a prospect added any T-Mobile product to cart - the strongest digital signal of purchase intent before checkout.' AS apx_definition,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_sum_warning,'add_to_cart_overall' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_actuals_overall' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nDERIVED TOTAL\nBASE METRIC\nLAYER 1\nLAYER 2\nLAYER 3 - CART START\nCART PAGE URLS\nCART PAGE NAMES\nBYOD CART PAGE\nLAYER 4\nCVR %\nREFRESH' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nAdd to Cart = Cart Postpaid Flow + Cart HSI Flow + Cart BYOD Flow. Flows CAN be summed - mutually exclusive product-type and page-scope filtering.\nCount of VISITS where a prospect performs a cart start action (scAdd or scOpen) on a recognized cart page.\nUniversal filters.\nProspect qualifiers: Exclude TMO Mobile Network Carrier + [sdi] Exclude Authenticated + [sdi] Exclude Visit Login Page + [DA] Exclude Single Page Visits.\n[sdi] cart start - requires a hit where scOpen OR scAdd exists AND page is a recognized cart page.\nwww.t-mobile.com/shopping-cart | www.t-mobile.com/cart | es.t-mobile.com/cart | es.t-mobile.com/shopping-cart.\nPage Name = "TMO:UNO | Shop : Cart" | "TMO | Shop : Cart" | "TLife App | Shop : Cart : Active Cart" | "TMO | Shop : Cart : Active Cart".\nPage Name = "TMO | Shop : Switch : Checkout Review" AND Cart Views (scView) exists AND Product Name (v35) = "BYOS SIM or eSIM".\nFlow-specific filters applied differently per sub-flow - see Cart flow rows.\nAdd to Cart / UPV Actuals.\nDaily at 7 AM PST.' AS apx_build_details,'PROSPECT FILTERS\nSUB-FLOW EXCLUSIONS' AS apx_excl_labels,'All prospect filters applied.\nFlow-specific exclusions detailed in each sub-flow row below.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 12 AS apx_sort_order,'cart_postpaid_flow' AS apx_id,'Cart - Postpaid Flow' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Mid Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,2 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Cart' AS apx_category,12 AS apx_category_sort,'Postpaid' AS apx_scope,'Postpaid' AS apx_lob,TRUE AS apx_is_subflow,'add_to_cart_overall' AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Improvado' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Visits in which a prospect started or added to a cart on the Postpaid path, with all HSI and BYOD cart activity removed.' AS apx_definition,'Sums with Cart HSI + Cart BYOD = Add to Cart total.' AS apx_sum_warning,'cart_postpaid_flow' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_postpaid_flow' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nLAYERS 1-3\nLAYER 4 - HSI CART EXCL\nHSI PRODUCT TYPE\nHSI FLOW NAME\nHSI URLS\nLAYER 4 - BYOD CART EXCL\nBYOD PRODUCT TYPE\nBYOD CHECKOUT PAGE\nBYOD FLOW NAME\nEXISTING CUSTOMER SCRUB\nCUSTOMER SIGNALS\nTRACKING CODES\nLOGIN SIGNALS\nSPRINT/CUSTOMER IND.\nCVR %' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nUniversal + Prospect + [sdi] cart start (same as Add to Cart overall).\n[sdi] Exclude HSI OR BYOD Cart Start - removes HSI cart activity from the Postpaid count.\nCart pages where Product Type (v100) = ISP.\nFlow Name (v154) = "AAL Intent" (HSI checkout initiation).\nURLs containing .t-mobile.com/home-internet/eligibility/base or /commerce/checkout/hint-order.\nRemoves BYOD cart activity from the Postpaid count.\nCart pages where Product Type (v100) = SIMCARDS.\n"TMO | Shop : Switch : Checkout Review" AND Cart Views (scView) exists AND Product Name (v35) = "BYOS SIM or eSIM".\nFlow Name (v154) starts with "DEFERRED Intent", "Prospect Activation", or "Activation Intent".\nAdditional scrub beyond Layer 2 for existing customer signals.\nMobile Carrier Network = T-Mobile | Encrypted MSISDN (v121) exists.\nTracking Code (v0) contains "_TMT_", "_C_", or "_CUST_".\nSuccessful Logins (e4) exists | Page contains web2go | Site Section = ma | Page URL (c3) contains my.t-mobile.com (excluding the login page itself).\nSite Name contains Sprint | Customer Indicators (v155) contains m:1 or b:1.\nCart Postpaid Flow / UPV Postpaid Flow. Sums with Cart HSI + Cart BYOD = Add to Cart total.' AS apx_build_details,'HSI AND BYOD CART\nCUSTOMER SIGNAL SCRUB' AS apx_excl_labels,'Removes HSI and BYOD cart actions from Postpaid count.\nAdditional existing-customer signal scrub: MSISDN, tracking codes, Sprint site, Customer Indicators.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
UNION ALL SELECT 13 AS apx_sort_order,'cart_hsi_flow' AS apx_id,'Cart - HSI Flow' AS apx_label,'Metric' AS apx_record_type,'Mid Funnel' AS apx_funnel_stage,2 AS apx_funnel_sort,'Cart' AS apx_category,13 AS apx_category_sort,'Home Internet (HSI)' AS apx_scope,'HSI' AS apx_lob,TRUE AS apx_is_subflow,'add_to_cart_overall' AS apx_parent_id,TRUE AS apx_subflows_summable,'Adobe Analytics -> Databricks (adobeFunnel pipeline)' AS apx_source_system,'Databricks' AS apx_source_platform,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly' AS apx_source_table,'Improvado' AS apx_data_owner,'Daily at 7 AM PST' AS apx_refresh_cadence,'Visits in which a prospect engaged with the Home Internet cart - indicating intent to purchase T-Mobile internet service.' AS apx_definition,'Part of Add to Cart total.' AS apx_sum_warning,'cart_hsi_flow' AS apx_cvr_numerator_id,'UPV_hsi_flow' AS apx_cvr_denominator_id,'SOURCE ARCHITECTURE\nLAYERS 1-2\nLAYER 3 - HSI CART\nCONDITION 1 - CART PAGE\nCONDITION 2 - PRODUCT\nCONDITION 3 - FLOW\nFLOW SIGNAL OPTIONS\nCVR %' AS apx_build_labels,'prdrzranalytics.lab42.sdi_tbl_adobeFunnel_gold_flowPerformanceByChannelGroups_weekly consolidates the individually migrated/ported Adobe funnel tables for each metric into one Gold table, so all Adobe funnel metrics live in a single place.\nUniversal + Prospect.\n[DA] HSI Prospect Cart Visits - includes HITS where ALL three conditions are true.\nPage URL (v6) contains .t-mobile.com/buy/cart or .t-mobile.com/cart | Page Name contains "TMO | HINT : Shop : Active Cart" or "TMO | Shop : Cart : Active Cart".\nProduct Type (v100) = ISP.\nVisit includes an active HSI prospect flow signal.\nFlow Name (v154) = "AAL Intent" | Page URL contains .t-mobile.com/home-internet/eligibility/base | Page URL contains .t-mobile.com/commerce/checkout/hint-order.\nCart HSI Flow / UPV HSI Flow. Part of Add to Cart total.' AS apx_build_details,'REQUIREMENT\nGENERAL HSI BROWSING' AS apx_excl_labels,'Requires ISP product type AND active HSI prospect flow signal.\nWill not fire for general HSI browsing without checkout intent.' AS apx_excl_details,CAST(NULL AS STRING) AS apx_glossary_category
